Dane Backbier - dbackbie - dbackbie@u.rochester.edu - Project 2 - Huffman Coding

Project 2 is an implementation of a Huffman coding tree, to both encode and decode
a file. Simply compile and run to test, making sure all the additional files (BinaryIn,
BinaryOut, and Huffman) are in the same directory as well as the original ur.jpg and
alice30.txt files.
The program will have worked if it successfully created a .enc file for both ur.jpg
and alice30.txt, a _dec.txt or _dec.jpg file for the corresponding file, which should
be identical with the original. If these files were all created correctly, then the
freq files must've also been made correctly since the creation of the output files
depend on the freq files.